# LF everywhere: in the repository and in the working tree, so a checkout on
# Windows round-trips byte-for-byte. This overrides core.autocrlf, which is
# set to true on this machine and would otherwise rewrite every text file to
# CRLF on checkout. The game reads .lua/.tl with either ending.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Exception. The in-game publisher writes this file itself, with CRLF, and the
# game reads it back to decide which mod.io mod a folder is. Keep the bytes
# exactly as published rather than normalising the line ending.
**/_metadata/mod.io_fileid.txt -text
